-- Passage rg4-word-parts-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b654ee9c-5516-5f64-accf-ac06a3ee8a71', 'rg4-word-parts-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Penguin Parents$q$, $q$Emperor penguins are flightless birds. They cannot fly, but they are skilled swimmers. They use their wings like flippers to zip through icy water.

In winter, the mother penguin lays a single egg. She passes it to the father and then walks to the sea to find food. The father keeps the egg warm on top of his feet, under a fold of skin. If the egg rolled onto the ice, it would be unprotected from the cold, and the chick inside could not survive.

For about two months, the fathers stand close together in a big group called a huddle. They take turns moving to the warm middle. During this time, they do not eat at all.

When the chick hatches, it is small and helpless. It cannot find food or keep itself warm. Soon the mother returns from the sea. She brings back a belly full of fish to feed her chick.

The parents take turns caring for the young penguin. By summer, the chick has grown new feathers and is ready to swim.$q$, 'draft')
