   $q$The prefix un- can mean "the opposite of," and a plug connects a device to power. What are "unplugged hours"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Time spent fixing broken wires and plugs","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Time spent away from phones and screens","is_correct":true},{"text":"Time spent watching shows on television","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Time spent charging every phone at home","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Time spent away from phones and screens$q$, $q$Unplugged is the opposite of plugged in, so it means a break from devices, which the passage calls a useful break. Charging phones keeps them plugged in, which is the opposite.$q$, 'draft', '41a71ab8-4fe3-542d-b83c-17d5b1515f9e')
